---
# Same pagination trick as home.njk / contract.njk.
pagination:
  data: pages.schedule.locales
  size: 1
  alias: locale
permalink: "{{ locale.permalink }}"
---
{#
  TAQATHON - WORKSHOPS PAGE TEMPLATE (src/pages/schedule.njk)
  ------------------------------------------------------------
  File/URL kept as "schedule" on purpose (this project's standing rule
  is never break a URL without a real reason — see the Phase 0 Eleventy
  migration entry in PROGRESS.md); the PAGE ITSELF was renamed
  "Workshops" and rebuilt as the site's primary destination when
  Taqathon 2026's hackathon was postponed in favor of a remote workshop
  series (2026-09-16 repositioning).

  Each workshop is now a card (date, time, title, speakers, a Sign Up
  button, a Join Session button) instead of a table row — see
  src/_data/copy/schedule.ar.json / schedule.en.json's "workshops"
  array for the data, and that file's own _comment for exactly which
  facts are real (the 3 real September 2026 sessions the user
  supplied, year confirmed 2026-09-16) vs. still unconfirmed (exact
  start times — each workshop's "time" renders the user's own "To Be
  Announced" placeholder, not a guess). Sign Up (signUpHref, a Google
  Form) and Join Session (meetingHref, a Google Meet link) render as
  disabled "pending" buttons for as long as their href is "#" — the
  exact same pattern registration.njk already uses for its own
  not-yet-real links — and become live buttons the moment a real URL
  replaces "#" in the copy files; the page-level ed-note below flags
  the same gap in prose for anyone who missed the disabled buttons.

  PUBLIC-VS-INTERNAL PASS (2026-09-16, same-day follow-up): the
  per-workshop "topics" list and "moderator" name are still present in
  the copy JSON (not deleted — same "hide, don't delete" rule as every
  other hidden thing on this site) but deliberately NOT rendered below
  anymore. The user clarified that level of detail (a slide-by-slide
  agenda outline, and who's running each session internally) was
  shared with this project as working/internal context, not copy meant
  to go out to the public — only date/title/time/speakers are meant to
  be public-facing. If a future round needs the topics or moderator
  back on the page, the data is still there; this file just needs its
  render loop restored (see the git history of this file for the
  original markup).

  The old hackathon-phase "keyDates" timeline (registration/screening/
  mentorship/winners) is NOT rendered below anymore — it described a
  competition timeline that no longer matches the current plan. Its
  data is still kept in the copy files rather than deleted, in case a
  version of it is needed again later.

  TO CUSTOMIZE:
    - Add/remove/reorder a workshop → edit the "workshops" array in the
      copy JSON files, NOT this file.
    - Headings/labels/intro → same copy JSON files.
#}
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}
{% block pageHead %}
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Big+Shoulders+Display:wght@600;700;800&family=Tajawal:wght@700;800;900&family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
{% endblock %}
{% block pageStyle %}
.sc-hero{ background:var(--color-cream); color:var(--brand-dark); padding:4rem 0 3rem; position:relative; overflow:hidden; border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,40,76,.08); }
.sc-hero::before{ content:""; position:absolute; top:-20%; inset-inline-end:-10%; width:420px; height:420px; background:radial-gradient(circle, rgba(196,64,26,.08), transparent 70%); border-radius:50%; pointer-events:none; z-index:0; }
.sc-hero .container{ position:relative; z-index:1; max-width:760px; text-align:center; }
.sc-display{ font-family:var(--font-display); font-weight:700; font-size:clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem); line-height:1; letter-spacing:-.01em; margin:0 0 1rem; }
[dir="rtl"] .sc-display{ font-family:'Tajawal', var(--font-display); font-weight:800; letter-spacing:0; }
.sc-intro{ color:var(--color-dust); font-size:1.05rem; margin:0; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .sc-hero{ color:var(--text); border-bottom-color:rgba(255,255,255,.08); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .sc-hero::before{ background:radial-gradient(circle, rgba(232,149,43,.10), transparent 70%); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .sc-intro{ color:var(--muted); }

.sc-section{ background:var(--color-sky); padding:3.5rem 0 4rem; }
.sc-section .container{ max-width:1080px; }

.ed-note{
  background:rgba(196,64,26,.05); border:1px solid rgba(196,64,26,.15); border-radius:.75rem;
  padding:1rem 1.25rem; display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:.75rem; color:var(--brand-dark);
  margin-bottom:1.5rem;
}
.ed-note .bi{ color:var(--color-terra); flex-shrink:0; margin-top:.15rem; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ed-note{ background:rgba(232,149,43,.06); border-color:rgba(232,149,43,.2); color:var(--text); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .ed-note .bi{ color:var(--color-amber); }

{#
  Workshop cards: same white-card-on-tinted-section pattern as every
  other page's content cards (registration.njk's .rg-card, the shared
  .card-lite convention) rather than inventing a new card treatment.
#}
.wk-card{
  background:#fff; border:1px solid rgba(0,40,76,.08); border-radius:1rem;
  padding:1.75rem; box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.04); height:100%;
  display:flex; flex-direction:column;
}
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .wk-card{ background:var(--surface); border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.08); box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.35); }
.wk-date{
  display:inline-block; align-self:flex-start; font-family:var(--font-mono-label);
  text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.06em; font-size:.7rem; font-weight:600;
  color:var(--color-terra); background:rgba(196,64,26,.08); border-radius:999px;
  padding:.3rem .7rem; margin-bottom:.85rem;
}
[dir="rtl"] .wk-date{ font-family:inherit; text-transform:none; letter-spacing:0; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .wk-date{ color:var(--color-amber); background:rgba(232,149,43,.12); }
.wk-title{
  font-family:var(--font-display); font-weight:700; color:var(--brand-dark);
  font-size:1.3rem; line-height:1.2; margin:0 0 .5rem;
}
[dir="rtl"] .wk-title{ font-family:'Tajawal', var(--font-display); font-weight:800; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .wk-title{ color:var(--text); }
.wk-time{ font-size:.85rem; color:var(--color-dust); margin-bottom:1rem; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .wk-time{ color:var(--muted); }
.wk-label{
  font-family:var(--font-mono-label); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.05em;
  font-size:.7rem; font-weight:600; color:var(--color-dust); margin-bottom:.5rem; display:block;
}
[dir="rtl"] .wk-label{ font-family:inherit; text-transform:none; letter-spacing:0; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .wk-label{ color:var(--muted); }
.wk-topics{ list-style:none; padding:0; margin:0 0 1.25rem; color:var(--brand-dark); }
.wk-topics li{ display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:.5rem; margin-bottom:.4rem; font-size:.92rem; }
.wk-topics li:last-child{ margin-bottom:0; }
.wk-topics .bi{ color:var(--color-terra); margin-top:.2rem; flex-shrink:0; font-size:.7rem; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .wk-topics{ color:var(--text); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .wk-topics .bi{ color:var(--color-amber); }
.wk-meta{ margin-top:auto; padding-top:1rem; border-top:1px solid rgba(0,40,76,.08); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .wk-meta{ border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.08); }
.wk-meta-row{ font-size:.88rem; color:var(--brand-dark); margin-bottom:.4rem; display:flex; gap:.4rem; }
.wk-meta-row:last-child{ margin-bottom:0; }
.wk-meta-row .bi{ color:var(--color-dust); margin-top:.15rem; }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .wk-meta-row{ color:var(--text); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .wk-meta-row .bi{ color:var(--muted); }

{#
  Sign-up/join buttons: same filled/outline pair already established
  by registration.njk (.rg-open-btn/.rg-copy-btn) and this page's own
  original .btn-join, reused here under this page's own "wk-" prefix
  rather than a third near-duplicate button style.
#}
.wk-actions{ margin-top:.6rem; }
.wk-btn-primary{ background:var(--color-amber); border:0; color:var(--brand-dark); font-weight:700; }
.wk-btn-primary:hover{ filter:brightness(1.05); color:var(--brand-dark); }
.wk-btn-outline{ border:1px solid rgba(0,40,76,.2); color:var(--brand-dark); background:transparent; }
.wk-btn-outline:hover{ background:rgba(0,40,76,.05); color:var(--brand-dark); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .wk-btn-outline{ border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.2); color:var(--text); }
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .wk-btn-outline:hover{ background:rgba(255,255,255,.06); color:var(--text); }
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

<section class="sc-hero">
<div class="container">
  <h1 class="sc-display">{{ locale.content.hero.heading }}</h1>
  <p class="sc-intro">{{ locale.content.intro }}</p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sc-section">
<div class="container">
  {% if locale.content.workshopsNote %}
  <div class="ed-note">
    <i class="bi bi-info-circle-fill"></i>
    <div>{{ locale.content.workshopsNote }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="row g-4">
    {% for w in locale.content.workshops %}
    <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6">
      <div class="wk-card">
        <span class="wk-date">{{ w.date }}</span>
        <h2 class="wk-title">{{ w.title }}</h2>
        {% if w.time %}
        <div class="wk-time"><i class="bi bi-clock {{ locale.content.iconMarginClass }}"></i>{{ locale.content.labels.time }}: {{ w.time }}</div>
        {% endif %}

        {#
          "topics" (a detailed session outline) and "moderator" are
          intentionally not rendered here — see this file's header
          comment (2026-09-16 public-vs-internal pass). Only speakers
          are shown.
        #}
        <div class="wk-meta">
          <div class="wk-meta-row">
            <i class="bi bi-mic {{ locale.content.iconMarginClass }}"></i>
            <span><strong>{{ locale.content.labels.speakers }}:</strong> {{ w.speakers | join(', ') }}</span>
          </div>

          {#
            Sign-up form + meeting link (2026-09-16 follow-up request):
            same "pending" pattern registration.njk already uses for its
            own not-yet-real links — href of "#" means no real URL
            exists yet, so it renders as a disabled button instead of a
            live one. Swap "#" for a real Google Form/Meet URL in the
            copy files and it becomes a live link automatically, no
            template change needed.
          #}
          <div class="wk-actions d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            {% if w.signUpHref and w.signUpHref != "#" %}
            <a class="btn btn-sm wk-btn-primary" href="{{ w.signUpHref }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <i class="bi bi-pencil-square {{ locale.content.iconMarginClass }}"></i>{{ locale.content.labels.signUp }}
            </a>
            {% else %}
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm wk-btn-primary" disabled aria-label="{{ locale.content.labels.signUpPendingAriaLabel }}">
              <i class="bi bi-pencil-square {{ locale.content.iconMarginClass }}"></i>{{ locale.content.labels.signUp }}
            </button>
            {% endif %}
            {% if w.meetingHref and w.meetingHref != "#" %}
            <a class="btn btn-sm wk-btn-outline" href="{{ w.meetingHref }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <i class="bi bi-camera-video {{ locale.content.iconMarginClass }}"></i>{{ locale.content.labels.join }}
            </a>
            {% else %}
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm wk-btn-outline" disabled aria-label="{{ locale.content.labels.joinPendingAriaLabel }}">
              <i class="bi bi-camera-video {{ locale.content.iconMarginClass }}"></i>{{ locale.content.labels.join }}
            </button>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>
</section>

{% endblock %}
